  "translation_rationale": "I modified Google Translate's suggestion to '數碼人文' as it is more idiomatic in Cantonese. '數位' (suhng yi) is a more common term used in Cantonese for 'digital', and '學術' (hok juk) is a more precise translation for 'humanities'. The combination of these two words accurately conveys the concept of Digital Humanities."
}

{
  "translated_term": "\(\n\)\( \) (déng-jī xué-shū)",
  "translation_rationale": "I used "" to represent the Minnan pronunciation of "" as /tɪŋ.ki/ and "" for "" which is equivalent to "" in Mandarin Chinese. I then added "" to make it clear that we're talking about the field of study, rather than just 'digital' in general."
}

