}

{
  "translated_term": "الإنسانيات الرقمية",
  "translation_rationale": "The term \"Digital Humanities\" is translated by combining the adjective \"إنساني\" (insāni), meaning humanistic or humanities, with \"رقمي\" (rumānī), meaning digital. The resulting phrase \"الإنسانيات الرقمية\" conveys the same meaning as the original English term."
}

{
  "translated_term": "hwrå nšy",
  "translation_rationale": "Using the Aramaic words \"hwr\" ( digital, from Hebrew דיגיטל, via Arabic ذکیطال) and \"nšy\" (humanities, from Greek humanities via Syriac \u0646\u062b\u0627\u0651\u06d0\u06cc\u0648\u0648\u062f\u0633\u0627\u0628\u0629)"
}

{
  "translated_term": "Digele Hwællicr Lēodhrycg",
  "translation_rationale": "The term is composed of two parts: 'Digele' (from Latin 'digitalis') and 'Hwællicr Lēodhrycg' (Humanities). 
  'Digital' is derived from the Latin 'digitalis', which was borrowed into Old English as 'digele'. 
  The word for humanities, 'Lēodhrycg', comes from the words 'lēod' meaning 'people' or 'nation' and 'hrycg' meaning 'knowledge' or 'learning'.
}

